IMPORT prelude
IMPORT properties

-- D2, re-read, then buy as a separate step. WRONG ON PURPOSE.
--
-- Alice and Bob each mean to buy dinner tonight, and neither wants to buy
-- it if the other already has. This design tries to fix D1 by asking the
-- ledger again just before buying: Alice checks, then reads the ledger
-- again, and buys if the second read said open. It narrows the window and
-- does not close it, because the re-read and the purchase are still two
-- steps: if Bob's purchase is recorded between them, two dinners are
-- bought. P1 is violated by re-read, Bob's purchase, buy.
--
-- A replay of Sequence A passes this design, because the 18:07 re-read
-- sees Bob's purchase of 18:06; only a search over every ordering finds
-- the window (the last trace below writes it by hand). Do not fix it; see
-- README.md.
--
-- Same shape as d1-naive.l4: one chain, one acting party, World, each act
-- naming its actor; a guard is a PROVIDED, an effect is a CONSIDER under
-- HENCE, the six variables are ledger cells (properties.l4). The re-read
-- carries whether the ledger answered: an unanswered re-read is the
-- brief's NoAnswer, a pause that changes nothing.

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `ledger records Bob's purchase`            -- BobBuys
    `Messages delivers the message`            -- Deliver
    `Alice checks whether dinner is bought`    -- CheckBought
    `Alice is done`                            -- Done
    `Alice reads the ledger again`             -- ReadAgain if answered, NoAnswer if not
        HAS `ledger answered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Alice buys dinner`                        -- Send
    `Alice gives up`                           -- AbandonR

`closing` MEANS 75600

§ `D2: the guards`

GIVEN act IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the brief allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `ledger records Bob's purchase`         THEN `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
    WHEN `Messages delivers the message`         THEN (RECALL Messages's `message`) EQUALS JUST `in transit`
    WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS planning
    WHEN `Alice is done`                         THEN `Alice has bought or stopped` (RECALL Alice's `plan`)
    WHEN `Alice reads the ledger again` answered THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS checked
    WHEN `Alice buys dinner`                     THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS reading
                                                      AND (RECALL Alice's `belief`) EQUALS JUST opened
    WHEN `Alice gives up`                        THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS reading
                                                      AND (RECALL Alice's `belief`) EQUALS JUST taken

§ `D2: the arrangement`

-- The arrangement opens with dinner unbought: the ledger's first record.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the arrangement` MEANS
    COMMIT `dinner status record` IS opened
    HENCE `the evening`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the evening` MEANS
    PARTY World
    MAY   act PROVIDED `the brief allows` act
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE CONSIDER act
          WHEN `ledger records Bob's purchase` THEN
              COMMIT `dinner status record` IS taken
              HENCE RECORD Messages's `message` IS `in transit`
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Messages delivers the message` THEN
              RECORD Messages's `message` IS delivered
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `belief` IS taken
              HENCE `Alice stops unless she has bought` (RECALL Alice's `plan`)
          WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN
              RECORD Alice's `belief` IS `the ledger's status` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS checked
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice is done` THEN `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice reads the ledger again` answered THEN
              IF answered
              THEN RECORD Alice's `belief` IS `the ledger's status` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
                   HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS reading
                   HENCE `the evening`
              ELSE `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice buys dinner` THEN
              COMMIT `dinners bought` IS `dinner for two`
              HENCE COMMIT `open at acceptance` IS `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS bought
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice gives up` THEN
              RECORD Alice's `plan` IS stopped
              HENCE `the evening`
    LEST  FULFILLED

-- The message stops Alice if she is still on her way to buying.
GIVEN plan IS A MAYBE Plan
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Alice stops unless she has bought` MEANS
    IF `Alice has bought or stopped` plan
    THEN `the evening`
    ELSE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS stopped
         HENCE `the evening`

§ `D2: the traces`

-- Read each trace's ledgers, not its FULFILLED line (d1-naive.l4 says why).

-- Sequence A, replayed on D2: the re-read at 18:07 sees Bob's purchase of
-- 18:06, the purchase is passed over, and Alice gives up. No dinner of
-- hers is recorded: this replay passes, and proves nothing about D2.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought`  AT 65100
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`          AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES (`Alice reads the ledger again` TRUE)    AT 65220
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                      AT 65225
    PARTY World DOES `Alice gives up`                         AT 65230
    PARTY World DOES `Messages delivers the message`          AT 65280
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)

-- The window: Alice re-reads at 18:05:50 and finds dinner open; Bob's
-- purchase is recorded at 18:06; Alice buys at 18:06:10 on what the
-- re-read told her. Official record: opened, taken, dinner for two, open
-- at acceptance FALSE. P1 is violated.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought`  AT 65100
    PARTY World DOES (`Alice reads the ledger again` TRUE)    AT 65150
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`          AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                      AT 65170
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)

-- The ledger does not answer twice (the pause, which changes nothing),
-- then answers open, and Alice buys before Bob. Official record: opened,
-- dinner for two, open at acceptance TRUE.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought`  AT 65100
    PARTY World DOES (`Alice reads the ledger again` FALSE)   AT 65110
    PARTY World DOES (`Alice reads the ledger again` FALSE)   AT 65120
    PARTY World DOES (`Alice reads the ledger again` TRUE)    AT 65125
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                      AT 65130
    PARTY World DOES `Alice is done`                          AT 65140
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)
